# Artifact-volume policy (Phase 160 D-15/D-16, recorded in full in IMAGE-PLAN.json's
# artifact_volume_policy). These are reproducible-from-the-record or too voluminous to be
# worth committing by default:
#   - written images are exactly reproducible from tools/gen_addr_image.py plus
#     IMAGE-PLAN.json's recorded size_bytes/mask/stamp_width, so their bytes stay local
#   - chip read-back run_*.bin files are ~6.5 MB total across the sweep; their SHAs are
#     recorded in EVIDENCE.jsonl, so a clean-match position is re-checkable by SHA alone
cells/*/reads/
cells/*/written.bin

# COMMITTED-ON-FAILURE EXCEPTION: for any position whose judged verdict is not a clean
# match (a SHA mismatch, an N=3 disagreement, or a verdict disagreement against the app's
# unjudged 0/1/2), the run_*.bin files and written.bin for THAT position must be committed
# -- Phase 165's root-cause analysis needs the actual bytes, not only their SHA. Because
# this .gitignore excludes them by default, committing a failing position's files requires
# the explicit escape hatch:
#     git add -f bench/cells/<cell_slug>/reads/run_01.bin  (etc.)
#     git add -f bench/cells/<cell_slug>/written.bin
